# Experience 1: Working at TD Bank

I started working at TD Bank while studying User Experience Design at Wilfrid Laurier University. My responsibilities included helping customers with their everyday banking needs, answering questions, and assisting them with different banking services. One thing I enjoyed about working at TD was interacting with different customers and helping them solve their problems. Through this experience, I learned how to communicate professionally, become more patient, and better understand customers' needs. One of my favourite memories was helping customers who struggled to use digital banking services, such as EasyWeb and the mobile banking app. It was rewarding to see customers become more confident after I helped them understand how to use these services. However, I do not enjoy dealing with frustrated customers, especially when their problems could not be solved immediately. These situations could be stressful, but they helped me improve my communication and problem-solving skills. Overall, I would give this experience an A because it helped me grow professionally and gain a better understanding of the financial industry. It also connects directly to my future goal of becoming a UX designer at TD Bank, where I hope to improve internally.
